## Why This Is Asked
This tests online adaptation capabilities with a minimal array configuration, handling non-stationary wind noise, and comparing per-bin versus joint diagonalization approaches under computational constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Online whitening with rolling covariance estimation
- 2x2 demixer update cadence and stability
- Per-bin ICA versus joint diagonalization trade-offs
- Cross-bin permutation strategies for small time-frequency representations
- Real-time evaluation frameworks for mobile hardware

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: Initialize W as identity, update W with gradient descent
let W = [[1, 0], [0, 1]];
for (let t = 0; t < frames.length; t++) {
  const whitened = whiten(frames[t]);
  const gradient = computeGradient(W, whitened);
  W = updateMatrix(W, gradient, learningRate);
}
```

